@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Unicode graphemes in terminal panes
+
+## What was broken
+
+The VTE parser delivers Unicode scalars one at a time. `Grid::add_character`
+previously discarded every scalar whose width was zero. A regression test showed
+`می‌روم` becoming `میروم`: U+200C ZERO WIDTH NON-JOINER was deleted. Accents,
+vowel marks, variation selectors and joiners were lost for the same reason.
+Emoji modifiers and regional indicators were instead stored as separate cells.
+
+## The change
+
+- A `TerminalCharacter` retains its first scalar and can additionally hold shared,
+  complete UTF-8 text. Unicode grapheme boundaries (`unicode-segmentation`), not
+  language-specific rules, decide whether another scalar extends the cell.
+  Zero-width format characters are also retained with the preceding cell.
+- The complete cell's width comes from `unicode-width`. The grid updates its
+  cursor and cached row width when a selector or other continuation changes it.
+  Extension happens before wrapping, so an accent at the right margin stays with
+  its base. A cluster that becomes wide at the margin can wrap as a whole.
+- Renderers, fake cursors, copy/selection, pane-content reports and dumps emit the
+  complete cell. Search matches scalar text but maps hits back to display cells;
+  regex highlights round partial-cluster matches out to the complete cell.
+- Completed cells keep their base character's style. A later style escape still
+  applies to subsequent cells. Repeating a character repeats the complete cell.
+
+A second bug appeared while testing arbitrary byte splits: VTE 0.15 can consume
+ASCII after a partially received UTF-8 scalar without printing it. The minimized
+case is `s\xcc` followed by `\xb6t\xcc\xb6` (the text `s̶t̶`). The pane's
+`advance_vte_bytes` helper feeds up to three initial continuation bytes separately,
+then processes the rest in a batch. All three pane parser entry points use it;
+forwarding/termination semantics are preserved and tested.
+
+## Coverage
+
+`zellij-server/src/panes/unit/fixtures/unicode_graphemes.txt` contains all 61
+original example lines, without normalization. Tests cover:
+
+- Exact text, display width, cursor position, copy, plain and ANSI dumps, search.
+- Every two-chunk byte split, including splits inside a UTF-8 scalar, with an
+  intervening render; actual pane input/rendering with six different chunk sizes.
+- Reflow and scrollback cell contents, late repaint, margins, overwrite, erase,
+  insert mode, style changes, repeat, shared-cell independence and output clipping.
+- Both positioned and newline output serializers; regex matches inside clusters.
+
+Useful commands (with native OpenSSL/zlib build dependencies available):
+
+```sh
+cargo test -p zellij-server --lib
+cargo fmt --all -- --check
+cargo build -p zellij --no-default-features
+```
+
+The no-default-features build is a local test executable, not an installation or
+replacement of a running Zellij session.
+
+## Scope and trade-offs
+
+- Terminal pane text only: this does not implement a shaping engine, font fallback,
+  Unicode bidi reordering, or grapheme-aware layout for every Zellij UI label.
+  Text remains in logical input order. Actual glyph appearance and agreement with
+  the width tables depend on the outer terminal. Automated tests are not visual
+  verification of every terminal/font combination.
+- A cell is now 24 rather than 16 bytes on x86-64. Single-scalar cells do not
+  allocate text; multi-scalar text is shared by clones. This has a scrollback
+  memory cost. No throughput or large-scrollback benchmark was performed.
+- Orphan zero-width scalars without a preceding cell are still ignored. If an
+  extension makes a cell too wide for the entire pane, or for the remaining space
+  with wrapping disabled, the existing cell is retained.
+- Case-insensitive and whole-word search retain their existing ASCII rules;
+  canonical-equivalence normalization is not added.
+- Existing screen-dump trimming of trailing spaces at soft-wrap boundaries is
+  unchanged. Reflow tests check the stored cells so this separate dump behavior
+  cannot conceal data loss in the grid.
